## Why This Is Asked

Assesses the ability to design scalable, isolation-driven E2E tests for multi-tenant SaaS platforms at scale, covering onboarding flows, live usage scenarios, and purge/audit compliance.

## Key Concepts

- Tenant isolation across services, data stores, and network boundaries
- Per-tenant feature flags and gradual rollout semantics
- Deterministic seeds, mocks, and observability mechanisms
- Data purge compliance, audit trail integrity, and cross-region considerations
- Cache and CDN boundary validation

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-harness seed function
async function seedTenantContext(tenantId, config) {
  const context = await testHarness.createContext({
    tenantId,
    featureFlags: config.flags,
    seedData: generateDeterministicSeed(tenantId)
  });
  return context;
}

// Cross-tenant leakage check
async function verifyTenantIsolation(tenantId, otherTenantId) {
  const tenantData = await db.query(`SELECT * FROM tenant_${tenantId}...`);
  const otherData = await db.query(`SELECT * FROM tenant_${otherTenantId}...`);
  expect(tenantData).not.toContain(otherData);
}
```

